Aroma: Earthy, mellow juniper and elderflower.
Flavours: Earthy flavours of lemon and citrus.
Type: Historically, it has been dominant in Sativa. However, testers claim it is a 50/50 hybrid.
Trim: Assorted medium to dense buds, slightly sticky.
Origin:   The strain's genetics  can be traced back to a number of sources, but most prominently, this  sativa is derived from South Asian and Jamaican landrace strains and cross-bred with Thai, Hawaiian, Jamaican, and Cambodian sativa .
Effect: The effects are difficult to assess but powerful nonetheless. Historically, this was known as a powerful strain, and one can easily overindulge because it is smooth and tasty. Please note that if you are purchasing it for personal use in countries where it is legal, consult your doctor before use .
Major Terpenes: Beta-Caryophyllene, Beta-Myrcene, D-Limonene
Unique Terpenes: Terpinolene, Guaiol

